# =====================================================================
# HARD RULE: no extracted game assets or data in git.
#
# This repository contains ONLY code we wrote. Nothing extracted from the
# .ipa may be committed: no textures, models, tables, terrain, sounds,
# no decoded/re-encoded copies of them, no JSON dumps of them, and no
# screenshots of the game rendering them. The decoders are ours; what
# they read and produce is not.
#
# Before committing, run:  python tools/check_no_assets.py
# See AGENTS.md "Asset hygiene".
# =====================================================================

# -- game data, in any form -------------------------------------------
*.ipa
*.bin
*.bdae
*.tbl
*.tga
*.pvr
*.trn
*.msk
*.shw
*.itm
*.wld
*.phy
*.beff
*.swf
*.wav
*.dds
*.ktx
*.pkm
*.astc
*.plist
*.nav
*.terrain
# The rest of an unpacked .ipa: interface files, string tables, the pack of
# interface words, and graph and data exports.
*.nib
*.strings
*.bar
*.graphml
*.sql
*.csv
# .svg is here because an .svg can carry a full base64 raster inside it, which
# the extension alone will not tell you. Ours are listed as exceptions below.
*.svg

# -- images and video: screenshots and decoded textures alike ---------
# Anything visual in this tree is a picture of, or made from, game data.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.webp
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mov
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mkv
# Narrow, reviewed exceptions, by exact file name. Each is mirrored in
# ALLOWED in tools/check_no_assets.py and has an entry in
# docs/IMAGES.md saying who made it and how.
!client/public/icons/icon-192.png
!client/public/icons/icon-512.png
!client/public/icons/icon-512-maskable.png
!client/public/icons/apple-touch-icon.png
!client/public/icons/favicon-16.png
!client/public/icons/favicon-32.png

# -- extracted / dumped data ------------------------------------------
# data/, Payload/ and extracted/ are where an unpacked .ipa or pack lands.
data/
Payload/
extracted/
*.glb
*.gltf
*.obj
*.fbx
*.dump
scene_check.json
work/*.json
work/cache/
work/shots/
work/*_out/
work/tex_check/
.cache/

# -- other packages, captures, archives, sound and fonts ---------------
# Fonts arrive through npm and are copied into the build; none is committed.
*.apk
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.har
*.zip
*.gz
*.tgz
*.bz2
*.7z
*.tar
*.rar
*.xz
*.dmg
*.jar
*.pak
*.ogg
*.mp3
*.aac
*.m4a
*.caf
*.aif
*.aiff
*.flac
*.mid
*.ttf
*.otf
*.woff
*.woff2
*.eot
*.sqlite

# -- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*

# -- build and tooling -------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.pytest_cache/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
nul
# Vite's on-disk dep cache. Regenerated on demand and machine-specific.
.vite/
client/.vite/

# Local HTTPS dev certs (mkcert). Machine-specific, includes a private key —
# never shared, never committed. See client/vite.config.ts.
client/.cert*/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# Ad-hoc diagnostic scripts at the repo root are scratch, not deliverables.
/check_*.py
/test_skeleton*.py

# Local notes kept beside the scratch scripts. Never committed.
work/bdae_docs/

# -- local scratch, never committed ------------------------------------
# work/ and debug/ are derivation scratch: one-off diagnostic scripts full of
# machine-specific absolute paths (including .ipa filenames). Their conclusions
# live in client/docs/formats/; the scripts themselves stay local. The portable
# test suite is client/test/.
work/
debug/
client/dev/zz_*
.claude/worktrees/

# Editor and OS state, which is not the project's.
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Local-only working notes and scanners.
local/
SWEEP-CLEANUP.md
